WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.425
The residual review classifies
everything a mover holds after the move.

2
00:00:04.425 --> 00:00:09.600
Take the lab's mover, from O R
G one hundred to O R G two ten.

3
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.325
The new department's
baseline is kept by rule.

4
00:00:12.325 --> 00:00:15.799
The old department's
baseline is removed by rule

5
00:00:15.799 --> 00:00:19.100
after the seven-day grace
period, by October 26.

6
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.249
Groups that sit behind a
package are package-managed,

7
00:00:22.249 --> 00:00:24.325
and a dynamic group is rule-managed.

8
00:00:24.325 --> 00:00:26.437
None of those need a person to decide.

9
00:00:26.437 --> 00:00:27.688
Two classes do.

10
00:00:27.688 --> 00:00:33.126
Access the mover requested, here a grants
reporting workspace, goes to review.

11
00:00:33.126 --> 00:00:38.800
And groups held outside packages, by direct
or nested assignment, go to review too.

12
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.112
Those are the items a rule can't see,
and they go to the manager of record.

13
00:00:43.112 --> 00:00:47.487
The time from the transfer to a
finished review is P S five's metric,

14
00:00:47.487 --> 00:00:51.600
and R V oh two flags a review
still open ten days after the move.
